    "ryouri (the food, a dish)",
    "ofuro (the bath)"
   ],
   "flags": [],
   "use": "Said to get people to the table (hayaku, samechau yo) or about a drink left too long (koohii sameta). Hosts say samenai uchi ni douzo (eat it while it's hot).",
   "notes": "samasu (let it cool) is the transitive partner. The sameru of me ga sameru (wake up) is a different word.",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "hayaku tabeyou, gohan samechau yo.",
    "ja": "早く食べよう、ご飯冷めちゃうよ。",
    "english": "Come on, let's eat, the food'll get cold."
   },
   "examplePolite": {
